A||||23||Slammed Fiero||Big Brake test results||||1||
Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||09-17-2001||03:57 PM||||Ok , as some of you know I have converted my car to 11.25" disc brakes all around (vented) with Camaro calipers and a blazer master cylinder. The pads are Wilwood polymatrix D street / semi race pad. The rotors are cryo treated by frozenrotors.com<P>I used a Vericom (expensive GTEC) to record the Data. The temp out right now is mid 60's. These stops are performed with Street tires on the front , R compounds on the back.<P>Stop #1: 125 Feet ...locked up the front<BR>Stop # 2 116 feet no lock up , brakes starting to warm up<BR>Stop # 3  109 Feet!!!!! Brakes nice and toasty, no fade<P><BR>This is on par with a Z06 , so needless to say I couldn't be happier. I think with the addition of a 4 piston caliper setup on the front I will be able to lower that number a bit more. I imagine with R compounds on the front , and a front mount battery I will be right at the 100ft mark.<P><BR>Happy Stopping.<P><BR>JM <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||09-17-2001||04:23 PM||||By that time you will need to reinforce your seat belts!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||09-17-2001||04:48 PM||||Wow!  Did you post pics/summary of your conversion somewhere?  I'd like to see them.  The brakes are the only thing I haven't touched on my car...yet.  Did you have to engineer much?  Does that test gizmo have a website?  I have a GTec, but I wonder about other devices.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
