Z||000010||Archie||09-18-2001||12:52 AM||||Very good!!! That is the same system I've been putting on several Fieros. Camaro Calipers on the front, Caddy calipers on the rear and LeBaron Rotors all around. I'm just running street tires and normal pads and rotors.<P>I first put them on my Chop Top Car..... then have put them on several cars since then.<P>I have them on my Finale and I can brake hard enough to raise the passenger completely out of the seat and against the seat belts.<P>I have been manufacturing the adapters for a couple of years. I'm just put a set on a customer car today and filmed a Video Instruction tape for them.<P>If I could figure out how to use my GTEC, I'd do some numbers too. I know for sure that setup is very effective.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000011||banditbalz||09-18-2001||10:23 AM||||I also bought a ticket and went for a ride in Slammedfieros machine. I could not imagine stopping any faster in ANY car. That bad boy needs a five point racing harness! I've got closeup pics of Slammedfiero's brake setup taken at our wedding. I will post in the next few days.<BR>_ <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||6
